The backend runs on the latest version of Python (3.13.2), so make sure
you have that installed.

Run the following command to install all of the requirements:
    pip install -r requirements.txt

To run the backend, run the following command:
    fastapi dev backend.py

Make sure that you have a .env file with values for GOOGLE_CX and GOOGLE_API_KEY.

Files:
    backend.py          Hosts API endpoints that can be queried.
    finder.py           Functions that do the actual fetching of data when there's
                        no data about a given person.

NOTE: See backend.test for the JSON data structure that stores all of the information
that has been found regarding a person. Do change the VERSION variable if you make
any changes to the structure.